Ohira

The Intelligence Layer for Modern Software.


---

Our Mission

Software projects are becoming too complex for humans and too fragmented for AI.

Developers spend countless hours explaining:

What the project does

The technology stack

Architecture decisions

Progress

APIs

Database models

Coding standards

Project history


Documentation becomes outdated.

AI assistants start every conversation with limited context.

New developers spend weeks understanding existing systems.

Ohira exists to solve this problem.

Our mission is to create a living intelligence layer that continuously understands software projects and makes that understanding available to developers, teams, and AI systems.


---

Our Vision

We envision a future where every software project has an intelligent knowledge layer.

Instead of reading thousands of files, developers and AI assistants can ask:

> "Explain this project."



And receive accurate, structured, and up-to-date answers.

Ohira becomes the universal bridge between software and intelligence.


---

Why We Exist

Modern software already has excellent tools:

Git stores history.

Docker manages infrastructure.

Prisma understands databases.

Frameworks organize applications.

CI/CD automates deployments.


Each tool understands only one part of a project.

None understands the project as a whole.

Ohira connects these pieces into one coherent understanding.


---

The Problem

Every software project accumulates knowledge:

Business rules

Architecture

APIs

Dependencies

Technical debt

Roadmaps

Documentation

Engineering decisions


Most of this knowledge is scattered across code, commits, documents, and developers' minds.

When someone leaves a team, much of that understanding leaves with them.

When an AI assistant starts helping, it must reconstruct the project from scratch.

This slows development and increases errors.


---

