---

Core Philosophy

Software Should Explain Itself.

Documentation should not become obsolete.

Architecture should not become hidden.

Knowledge should not disappear when developers leave.

AI should not repeatedly rediscover the same project.

Ohira makes software understandable.


---

Core Principles

1. Framework Agnostic

Ohira supports projects regardless of technology stack.

Whether the project uses:

Next.js

Node.js

Laravel

Django

Flutter

React Native

Spring Boot

Go

Rust

.NET


the experience remains consistent.


---

2. AI First

Everything produced by Ohira is designed to be easily consumed by AI systems.

Rather than exposing raw code, Ohira provides structured knowledge.


---

3. Plugin First

Everything is a plugin.

Support for technologies, databases, cloud providers, authentication systems, and deployment platforms is delivered through modular plugins.

This keeps the core lightweight and extensible.


---

4. Open by Design

Ohira should encourage community contributions.

Developers should be able to create plugins, collectors, analyzers, and integrations without modifying the core.


---

5. Knowledge over Files

Ohira focuses on understanding relationships instead of simply listing files.

It models:

Projects

Features

Modules

Services

APIs

Databases

Dependencies

Workflows


rather than folders alone.


